# recursive_union.tkr — the §9.D CR1 ACCEPT host: a RECURSIVE inline union `TInt | TArr | null` whose
# `TArr.elem` field carries the whole union by value. Codegen boxes that by-value back-edge as a heap
# pointer (`tk_u_<keys> *`, anchored on the forward-declarable typedef) exactly as the named variant it
# replaces already did, so the C struct stays finite. Each scenario names itself and asserts its
# announced value through `run` in `main.tks`. Inert on the seed until a recursive inline union exists:
# this is the additive "teach the compiler to box recursion" capability (owner ruling, option 1).

Feature: recursive_union — §9.D CR1 boxing of a recursive inline union member

  Scenario: arr_depth — a three-deep TArr(TArr(TArr(TInt))) reads its nesting depth back through the boxed elem chain (→ 3)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario arr_depth: ok"

  Scenario: null_member — a TArr { elem = null } round-trips the null case seated in a multi-member inline-tag union through the box (→ 7)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario null_member: ok"

  Scenario: payload — descending two boxed elem hops reads the innermost TInt.bits back intact (→ 42)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario payload: ok"
